gh `S_R`. It does not establish that the issuer did not create other instances for the same `claim_digest` under different `request_id` values, bind those instances to different profiles or world classes, or select the presented instance after observing evidence or outcomes."},{"bridge":"`CompatibleÏ€`","id":"BRIDGE_01","lean_checks":"The frozen relation returns `true` for (e, wâ‚€) and (e, wâ‚)","remaining_limitation":"Whether the relation faithfully represents real-world compatibility","source":"P10 profile v0.1.1 Â§3 semantic-bridge table, row 1 (verbatim cells)"},{"bridge":"`EvalÏ€`","id":"BRIDGE_02","lean_checks":"The frozen function returns different values on wâ‚€ and wâ‚","remaining_limitation":"Whether `EvalÏ€` faithfully translates the natural-language claim; this is P10 `R_sem` unless the claim is already formal","source":"P10 profile v0.1.1 Â§3 semantic-bridge table, row 2 (verbatim cells)"},{"bridge":"`EÏ€` and admission","id":"BRIDGE_03","lean_checks":"`e âˆˆ EÏ€` under the frozen rules","remaining_limitation":"Whether `EÏ€` realistically covers obtainable evidence","source":"P10 profile v0.1.1 Â§3 semantic-bridge table, row 3 (verbatim cells)"},{"bridge":"Profile adequacy (AP1)","id":"BRIDGE_04","lean_checks":"`FormallyUnderdeterminationCapable(Ï€, c)`","remaining_limitation":"Whether the determining evidence fixture is practically obtainable and representative (limitation below)","source":"P10 profile v0.1.1 Â§3 semantic-bridge table, row 4 (verbatim cells)"},{"bridge":"Canonicalization / codec","id":"BRIDGE_05","lean_checks":"SHA-256 digest and JCS canonical form match","remaining_limitation":"Whether canonicalization loses claim-relevant information","source":"P10 profile v0.1.1 Â§3 semantic-bridge table, row 5 (verbatim cells)"},{"bridge":"Replay/order","id":"BRIDGE_06","lean_checks":"The complete VDS prefix of committed L reconstructs `S_R` and registration order (Â§2.4)","remaining_limitation":"Authorized access to all leaf/protected-header data and required subject payloads; registration order is not issuance order; other logs are outside the claim","source":"P10 profile v0.1.1 Â§3 semantic-bridge table, row 6 (verbatim cells)"},{"bridge":"Within-batch order","id":"BRIDGE_07","lean_checks":"Committed leaf indices define one total registration order","remaining_limitation":"The TS chooses within-batch leaf order; an order-sensitive `BundleÏ€` therefore treats that TS choice as an explicit trust assumption","source":"P10 profile v0.1.1 Â§3 semantic-bridge table, row 7 (verbatim cells)"},{"bridge":"Pre-evidence commitment","id":"BRIDGE_08","lean_checks":"Profile and instance were registered before protocol admission (Â§Â§2.3â€“2.5)","remaining_limitation":"Does not prove author ignorance of public data or absence of other instances","source":"P10 profile v0.1.1 Â§3 semantic-bridge table, row 8 (verbatim cells)"},{"bridge":"Active profile/verifier","id":"BRIDGE_09","lean_checks":"`ActiveProfileBindingV0` resolves the unique instance-bound profile and verifies the certificate using only the checker, build, axiom policy, codecs, dependencies, `.olean` files, and Lean toolchain transitively bound by that profile","remaining_limitation":"Establishes verifier-time recomputation under the committed adjudication profile; it does not establish that a downstream action was governed by the verdict","source":"P10 profile v0.1.1 Â§3 semantic-bridge table, row 9 (verbatim cells)"},{"bridge":"Coverage","id":"BRIDGE_10","lean_checks":"`EvidenceClosure` and `CoverageProof` close all valid, registered, in-scope admissions by authorized admitters through `S_R` (Â§2.6)","remaining_limitation":"Does not prove absence of unregistered/out-of-scope evidence, another `request_id`, or future entries","source":"P10 profile v0.1.1 Â§3 semantic-bridge table, row 10 (verbatim cells)"},{"bridge":"Cryptography","id":"BRIDGE_11","lean_checks":"Digests and signatures match","remaining_limitation":"Digest collision resistance, signature unforgeability, and log non-equivocation/integrity","source":"P10 profile v0.1.1 Â§3 semantic-bridge table, row 11 (verbatim cells)"},{"bridge":"Verifier","id":"BRIDGE_12","lean_checks":"Kernel type-check plus `#print axioms` audit; the permitted axiom set is explicit in the profile","remaining_limitation":"Trust in the Lean kernel and declared axioms; `sorryAx`, `Lean.ofReduceBool`, and `native_decide` are forbidden","source":"P10 profile v0.1.1 Â§3 semantic-bridge table, row 12 (verbatim cells)"}],"limitations_digest":"7c9252664b112621087d0a74b3f8fd5ec50f9ed912cc0d1a611bc227d3d15214","log_identity_digest":"d3a258a755e554970cb94cf9f23adb015a91440815c97417e37a6e68c5c0354c","must_understand":["limitations"],"outcome":{"kind":"NotDemonstrated","reason":"underdetermined"},"preclosure_transcript_digest":"69b9f0f5ae067b4a96beed153842299bb0194f9ca6da31fc23f29fb75d6e20a6","profile_commitment_ref":"2","proof_digest":"30f498438473d39566d951b75dd5ce7326d9c368da3cda4868635a3e422a8696","verifier_digest":"f8380b19b43334925e7f7621e1f7d7912f36c789199d3f8d069b87f5ea176d46","witness_0_digest":"15304eb2956a2f07fbf4028dfd7f421c99f9a03da473fec9d75b997132747f32","witness_1_digest":"6fc3108dc0bf1f6cf7fe5df39b513c3b7be7312111a0ef0c4a05839194db5d5b"},"predicateType":"https://volmax-studio.rs/p10/predicate/adjudication/v0.1","subject":[{"digest":{"sha256":"e4e2beb8a29d6b77ef4c52bbdd1eea64c38fe8e75b58f3d9db50231f217a0bf0"},"name":"p10s2sub:0fe1be115beb770330930911e69e4f2026c80809c64ada16e87fe63e7f9150d2"}]}X@…¾5,”Î¾^Wë	RúW™/5„-4’Wi&”€-5MXÜõZşŒqM²5j„=×İô˜ZæsX	ˆ‚␀Y
